<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21002" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hospĭtālĭtas</span></b> ,
			ātis, f.
		hospitalis. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Hospitality</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">recte etiam a Theophrasto est laudata
					hospitalitas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Off. 2, 18, 64</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Mart. 4, 64, 28</span></i>.—*
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A being a guest</i>, i. e. <i>a living
				in a foreign country</i>, <i>a sojourning</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lege temporalis hospitalitatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. Somn. Scip. 1, 21, §
				34</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
